WEBVTT

00:00:00.583 --> 00:00:03.482
A strong advanced SQL solution includes reasoning.

00:00:03.482 --> 00:00:06.082
Sequenced is still one row per admission.

00:00:06.082 --> 00:00:10.202
Intervals is one row per admission that has a previous encounter.

00:00:10.202 --> 00:00:15.367
The final output keeps that repeat-admission grain while adding a name and classification.

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:20.267
Being able to explain these stages is more important than memorizing the exact query.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:24.737
Connect this idea to a hospital ranking visits and identifying readmissions.

00:00:24.737 --> 00:00:29.437
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:29.437 --> 00:00:36.507
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:36.507 --> 00:00:40.212
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:46.001
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
